(1375271, 172325, 15982, '<td valign="top">I think a tighter frame from just the "Geno''s Steaks" up would have made for a more interesting shot and take some of the choas from the bottom away - my eye wonders around a little much there. But I think this is quite good for such a busy picture!</td>', 'I think a tighter frame from just the "Geno''s Steaks" up would have made for a more interesting shot and take some of the choas from the bottom away - my eye wonders around a little much there. But I think this is quite good for such a busy picture!', '2005-05-10 11:57:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1375277, 173819, 27789, '<td valign="top">i love all the different colors and the cloud, great capture</td>', 'i love all the different colors and the cloud, great capture', '2005-05-10 12:01:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1375280, 173509, 27789, '<td valign="top">great abstract, one of my favorite of the challenge</td>', 'great abstract, one of my favorite of the challenge', '2005-05-10 12:03:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1375282, 172546, 15982, '<td valign="top">I like the idea for this picture and the background is great! The focus on your subject seems too soft here though. And I probably would have gotten the camera lower to get a closer shot on your subject and keep the interesting lights and reflections in the background. I think the flash could either be a good thing to balance the color cast from the lights, or a bad thing taking away from the overall mood of the picture. I personally perfer natural lighting when possible, but this is definitely a tricky shot to get the white balance right. But it looks like the pole your subject is stiing in front of became the focal point in your camera''s AF. That''s one of the tricky things about night shots is getting the focus right!! Good luck! 6</td>', 'I like the idea for this picture and the background is great! The focus on your subject seems too soft here though. And I probably would have gotten the camera lower to get a closer shot on your subject and keep the interesting lights and reflections in the background. I think the flash could either be a good thing to balance the color cast from the lights, or a bad thing taking away from the overall mood of the picture. I personally perfer natural lighting when possible, but this is definitely a tricky shot to get the white balance right. But it looks like the pole your subject is stiing in front of became the focal point in your camera''s AF. That''s one of the tricky things about night shots is getting the focus right!! Good luck! 6', '2005-05-10 12:04:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1375284, 173222, 15982, '<td valign="top">I can''t identify the theme of the challenge in this photo. It may have been taken at night, but there is nothing here that says "Late Night" in my opinion.</td>', 'I can''t identify the theme of the challenge in this photo. It may have been taken at night, but there is nothing here that says "Late Night" in my opinion.', '2005-05-10 12:06:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1375290, 172604, 15982, '<td valign="top">I love this picture! I think if the camera was turned a little so that the poles had a little more diagonal cut across the picture it would have been more interesting - and maybe a little more exposure on the chain the bring out its texture better. But this is a great photo!</td>', 'I love this picture! I think if the camera was turned a little so that the poles had a little more diagonal cut across the picture it would have been more interesting - and maybe a little more exposure on the chain the bring out its texture better. But this is a great photo!', '2005-05-10 12:10:02.000000', NULL, 1),
