(1377353, 173296, 37215, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the votes - This was my first challenge so I am thrilled with the result, grateful for the helpful comments and excited about future pictures. So pleased to have found DP site. It''s great!</td>', 'Thank you for the votes - This was my first challenge so I am thrilled with the result, grateful for the helpful comments and excited about future pictures. So pleased to have found DP site. It''s great!', '2005-05-11 04:57:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1377363, 173745, 27137, '<td valign="top">Funny to see the amount of votes comments you got.. never so much for a ''last'' photo :))<br/></td>', 'Funny to see the amount of votes comments you got.. never so much for a ''last'' photo :))', '2005-05-11 05:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1377398, 173399, 21669, '<td valign="top">Great work - well done indeed</td>', 'Great work - well done indeed', '2005-05-11 05:37:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1377422, 173763, 23394, '<td valign="top">sweet shot, adi!  congrats on your best score, year-to-date!<br/> <br/>now...go back and reshoot it at iso100 at the highest f-stop your camera will allow for the longest correct exposure your camera will allow.  if you don''t have a tripod, take/find something to rest the camera on (and if you don''t have a tripod, get a small bag and fill it with beans or rice).  once you''re set up, put the camera in timer mode so you won''t get any camera shake from pressing the shutter.  lastly, if your camera supports it, shoot it raw.  try these things, and you will be absolutely amazed at how those lines come in razor sharp.<br/> <br/>as for everything else, the composition, lighting, and framing are wonderful.  i wouldn''t change a thing.  good work!</td>', 'sweet shot, adi!  congrats on your best score, year-to-date! now...go back and reshoot it at iso100 at the highest f-stop your camera will allow for the longest correct exposure your camera will allow.  if you don''t have a tripod, take/find something to rest the camera on (and if you don''t have a tripod, get a small bag and fill it with beans or rice).  once you''re set up, put the camera in timer mode so you won''t get any camera shake from pressing the shutter.  lastly, if your camera supports it, shoot it raw.  try these things, and you will be absolutely amazed at how those lines come in razor sharp. as for everything else, the composition, lighting, and framing are wonderful.  i wouldn''t change a thing.  good work!', '2005-05-11 05:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1377445, 173781, 27482, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your best score so far, now keep it up and go get that ribbon wich I personally thought you deserved for this picture.</td>', 'Congrats on your best score so far, now keep it up and go get that ribbon wich I personally thought you deserved for this picture.', '2005-05-11 06:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
