(1386090, 173120, 35513, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dahkota:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent capture.  Reminds me of Edward Hoppers "Nighthawks." Pulling in a little closer would have really put it there!  Exposure really well done - excellent job not blowing out the lights but still leaving the dark parts viewable. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!  That''s exactly the look I was going for :-)  Wish I had found NeatImage BEFORE this contest entry, but ah well.  A closer shot probably would be a good idea...my eye doesn''t always catch up with my ideas ;-)  I''ll have to see if I can revisit and get a closer pic.</td>', 'Originally posted by dahkota: Excellent capture.  Reminds me of Edward Hoppers "Nighthawks." Pulling in a little closer would have really put it there!  Exposure really well done - excellent job not blowing out the lights but still leaving the dark parts viewable.   Thank you!  That''s exactly the look I was going for :-)  Wish I had found NeatImage BEFORE this contest entry, but ah well.  A closer shot probably would be a good idea...my eye doesn''t always catch up with my ideas ;-)  I''ll have to see if I can revisit and get a closer pic.', '2005-05-14 21:09:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1386758, 173645, 30881, '<td valign="top">This image really did it for me. It has that empty lonely 4 in the morning feel to it, that you sometimes get when walking around downtown in a city.<br/>Glad it was people free (more deserted feeling!) I gave it a 10. Every photo community is bombarded with city night scapes(getting really tiresome) Glad to see your imagination at work Great Job!</td>', 'This image really did it for me. It has that empty lonely 4 in the morning feel to it, that you sometimes get when walking around downtown in a city.Glad it was people free (more deserted feeling!) I gave it a 10. Every photo community is bombarded with city night scapes(getting really tiresome) Glad to see your imagination at work Great Job!', '2005-05-15 12:32:16.000000', NULL, 0),
